#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:5
#: cba3cae28aa84226b01f766578a0c0fd
msgid "UAV LogViewer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:7
#: c6f012e249674b9ca9968b96bb67e1ce
msgid "This utility provides an easy to use viewer for ArduPilot dataflash and telemetry logs. Data can be plotted and even manipulated, and the flight visually re-flown in 3D. It is accessed `HERE <http://plot.ardupilot.org>`__ and is web based, although most of the computations are done locally in the web browser. Both Chrome/Chromium and FireFox are supported browsers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:11
#: 8e6794e4d6c94e71bdf6805564191b3f
msgid "Initial Screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:15
#: 974799cbfae748d58f805590a47c3ea5
msgid "Upon accessing, this panel is presented. You can \"Open (a) Sample\" file to experiment with, or load an ArduPilot .tlog or .bin  log file, either by drag and drop or by clicking to obtain a file explorer dialog to select the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:19
#: 779d3ae533974433ab993a86014f8d1a
msgid "Main Screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:21
#: 68267df34cda43f48b20c1ec8eb3b359
msgid "Once a log is loaded, if it has GPS data, it will display this screen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:26
#: 2403d60539924b65a2359b09333fd88f
msgid "which is the 3D flight viewer. You can replay the flight in 3D by pressing the \"play\" button, or \"pause\", \"reverse\", or  change playback \"speed\". Various map tools/options are in the upper right corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:28
#: d690af70d6bd486e8fd6bf8bd12a8865
msgid "In the upper left are setup menu buttons for the Plot (whose options are shown already), 3D panel, and additional widgets for parameters, log messages, and a joystick visualizer for the first four RC channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:31
#: 1fb4e88ffd934164965b4adfec5b1418
msgid "3D View Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:37
#: cd2def747acd4ee3b8b91d85fdcc759a
msgid "In this panel, you can change the camera mode in 3D playback, if waypoints and/or trajectory is shown, the size of the vehicle in the display, and the data source used for showing the trajectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:40
#: 0f8d59d043004cc68ca675e72c763b90
msgid "Plot Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:45
#: 8503384a622e4abeb6396229e5693110
msgid "This is one of the most powerful features of the viewer. This allows you to select which log values are plotted. You can search for an individual field to  plot, eg for CTUN.NavRoll you would type \"Nav\") or just navigate thru to the message with that field. Here we have plotted CTUN.NavRoll, CTUN.Roll,CTUN.NavPitch, and CTUN.Pitch.The Navigation controller's desired roll and pitch versu actual. ( For a complete list of log messages, see: `Copter Log Messages <https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/logmessages.html>`__ , `Plane Log Messages <https://ardupilot.org/plane/docs/logmessages.html>`__ , or `Rover Log Messages <https://ardupilot.org/rover/docs/logmessages.html>`__ )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:48
#: 0937915a026f4669abee5d2ed8846713
msgid "Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:50
#: 84e610ab138a47ef83ae8c9cf808c266
msgid "Above the \"Plot Individual Field\" dropdown, is a \"Presets\" dropdown with many commonly used combinations of data plots already pre-configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:53
#: be5810e8f64545a3b4de5740b62effd8
msgid "Plot Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:55
#: c5febd5f4fd64cbe9b1475ff08927971
msgid "When each field is added, a Y axis number is assigned, and the data autoscaled and centered. This can be changed by hovering over the axis and scrolling to change scale, or clicking and moving the origin. If you wish to automatically align and scale several fields to one another, just set the y axis number to be the same. They will remain together from that point on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:57
#: 525bffee573a418681ac9c88cb18e72a
msgid "You can change the color code by clicking the color swatch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:59
#: d14cff94fabe4b56b2134c671a3f9deb
msgid "You can remove a data plot by clicking the trash can icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:61
#: cee8486be68b4fabb24813c5ecf7362a
msgid "You can even create and plot expressions that use the fields by \"Add Expression\" button. See `Graph Expressions for MavExplorer <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/using-mavexplorer-for-log-analysis.html#graph-expressions>`__ for examples of using expressions in a plot analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:63
#: b63b70b4b6514610b77cb90e4c0adc55
msgid "You can also save the present plot and its setup using the \"Save Preset\" button. These are persistent from session to session. A preset can be removed by tbd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:65
#: ec2965caafe14188b0fb05e0f764950e
msgid "Using the slider bars on the timeline under the main graphs, you can narrow or expand the plot region of the lob and move its center on the log timeline. Note that the 3D graph follows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:67
#: fc56c3bfc372485ea1e8f99d59f99bef
msgid "The mouse cursor will move the 3D plot's time position. It can also show the exact values of each plot line at its current position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:69
#: c28e82af7f024048932f08a989106219
msgid "You can dismiss the 3D screen by clicking in the X box in its upper right corner. The entire right side will now be devoted to the plots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:76
#: fb88992df2c14e07bd3eaeed1d325090
msgid "If you move the mouse to the upper right corner of the plot screen, several options will become visible. You can take a snapshot of the plot area, re-auto scale, zoom, move, change what values appear with the mouse cursor, toggle x/y lines that move with cursor position, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:79
#: 8e8b41058f17409ebe7ec904e396aa64
msgid "Widgets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:81
#: acfc19acd4fb463492c4a6028c322632
msgid "Three widgets are available when you click the widgets menu at the top left of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavlogviewer.rst:87
#: 2e14b169e17f4b7badc28a86a9cb74ef
msgid "These are sizable (bottom right corners) and movable (upper left corner) panels that display the log messages up to the cursor point, the joystick positions (first 4 rc channels), and a searchable parameter list. These can be shown or dismissed with their buttons when in this setup menu. Click \"Plot\" or \"3D\" to return to those screens."
msgstr ""
